<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><p:notes xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" xmlns:p="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/presentationml/2006/main"><p:cSld><p:spTree><p:nvGrpSpPr><p:cNvPr id="1" name=""/><p:cNvGrpSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvGrpSpPr><p:grpSpPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="0" cy="0"/><a:chOff x="0" y="0"/><a:chExt cx="0" cy="0"/></a:xfrm></p:grpSpPr><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="2" name="Notes body"/><p:cNvSpPr txBox="1"/><p:nvPr><p:ph type="body" idx="1"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="685800" y="914400"/><a:ext cx="5486400" cy="7315200"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr wrap="square" lIns="0" rIns="0" tIns="0" bIns="0" anchor="t"/><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr algn="l"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="105000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="300"/></a:spcAft><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1200" b="0" i="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="222B31"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Arial"/><a:ea typeface="Arial"/><a:cs typeface="Arial"/></a:rPr><a:t xml:space="preserve">Policy is a pure decision function over a typed Candidate and immutable EvidenceSnapshot. It first rejects ACL-denied, authority-denied or exact unsafe-use candidates. A separately safe finding provides only an exact content/use/policy exception from reputation; it cannot raise original authority or permissions. R then has no sibling effect. C uses full-history contributor/context counts. M always considers batch, context and contributor maxima and therefore controls for receiving the richer metadata. S considers the maximum only among supported scopes. Group overlaps are not combined as independent probabilities. An active scope does not invent a new safety label for its members. Recent-four history C and fixed convex-mixture M variants are specified for an expanded study but not implemented in this minimum evaluation. We do not report A-MemGuard or other paper-baseline rows as run if they were not faithfully adapted.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="1200"/></a:p><a:p><a:pPr algn="l"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="105000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="300"/></a:spcAft><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1200" b="0" i="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="222B31"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Arial"/><a:ea typeface="Arial"/><a:cs typeface="Arial"/></a:rPr><a:t xml:space="preserve"></a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="1200"/></a:p><a:p><a:pPr algn="l"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="105000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="300"/></a:spcAft><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1200" b="0" i="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="222B31"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Arial"/><a:ea typeface="Arial"/><a:cs typeface="Arial"/></a:rPr><a:t xml:space="preserve">SOURCES</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="1200"/></a:p><a:p><a:pPr algn="l"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="105000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="300"/></a:spcAft><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1200" b="0" i="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="222B31"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Arial"/><a:ea typeface="Arial"/><a:cs typeface="Arial"/></a:rPr><a:t xml:space="preserve">- src/ams/research/dynamic/policies.py</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="1200"/></a:p><a:p><a:pPr algn="l"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="105000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="300"/></a:spcAft><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1200" b="0" i="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="222B31"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Arial"/><a:ea typeface="Arial"/><a:cs typeface="Arial"/></a:rPr><a:t xml:space="preserve">- reports/MPBENCH_DYNAMIC_EXPERIMENT_PROTOCOL.md §9.2</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="1200"/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp></p:spTree></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:notes>